        "original_id": "2b4fe2e6-7ba4-5f2a-9a41-e79ce494b52c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Trembling Before G-d, Zeitgeist film series, A Jihad for Love\n- People: Sandi Simcha DuBowski, Parvez Sharma\n- Topics: LGBT people and religion, Orthodox Judaism, conspiracy theories, social and economic change\n\nFacts:\n- Trembling Before G-d is a 2001 American documentary film about gay and lesbian Orthodox Jews trying to reconcile their sexuality with their faith.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski is an American director and producer known for work about the intersection of LGBT people and religion.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski directed the 2001 documentary Trembling Before G-d.\n- Zeitgeist is a series of three documentary films released between 2007 and 2011 that present conspiracy theories and proposals for broad social and economic changes.\n- Parvez Sharma directed the 2007 documentary A Jihad for Love, which was formerly known as In the Name of Allah.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski was the producer of Parvez Sharma's 2007 documentary A Jihad for Love.",
